<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <POU Name="FB_ConveyorTests" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000001}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Suite over FB_Conveyor: every arc of the drawn six-state machine, the two
    overrides that end a run from wherever it is, and everything the module
    publishes while it walks them.

    WHERE EACH ARC IS PINNED, AND WHY IT IS SPLIT AT ALL

    xStunit's simulated clock is driven from the C# harness and has no
    ST-visible advance, so a suite written in ST sees time frozen. Four arcs of
    this machine are gated on a timer, and each one is covered from BOTH sides:

      Start -> STARTING -> WAIT_CONTAINER          gated on AccelTime
      STOPPING -> INIT                             gated on DecelTime
      PROCES_CONTAINER -> WAIT_CONTAINER           gated on the drawn Delay
      the belt run-on after the demand drops       gated on MotorRunOn

    From here, with the clock stopped, both ENDS of each of those gates are
    exact and need no clock at all. At zero the gate is transparent and the arc
    is taken on the scan it becomes available, which is what lets this suite
    walk the whole machine; at any non-zero setting no window can ever close,
    so the arc must not be taken however many cycles are run. What happens
    strictly BETWEEN those ends - the boundary scan a window actually closes on,
    and a window restarting rather than resuming - is pinned in
    tests/xStunit.Interpreter.Tests/Miniload/ConveyorTimingTests.cs, against
    these same fixture files with the harness moving the clock.

    Everything else here - detection, the downstream handshake in both
    directions, the Stop override, the fault latch, the counter, the speed
    scaling and the published sensor snapshot - is decided by CALLS rather than
    by elapsed time and lives wholly in ST.

    The detection point is a real FB_DigitalInput from the sensor fixture
    directory, running in simulation with its debounce off, rather than a
    stand-in written for this suite: an equipment module that only works
    against a mock of its own leaf is not evidence about the machine.

    The dependencies and the recipe are bound on the FIRST call of each case
    and left standing; a later bare conveyor() is therefore one more scan with
    nothing changed, and a named argument in a later call is the one level that
    case is moving.
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_ConveyorTests EXTENDS TcUnit.FB_TestSuite]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[ConveyorPowersUpStoppedWithNothingCounted();
StartRampsTheConveyorUpToWaitingForAContainer();
ANonZeroAccelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStarting();
DetectionHoldsTheContainerUntilDownstreamIsReady();
DownstreamReadyReleasesTheContainerIntoTheHandover();
AWithdrawnDownstreamPutsTheContainerBackOnHold();
AContainerLiftedOffTheEyeReleasesTheHold();
AClearedEyeCompletesTheHandoverAndCountsTheContainer();
AContainerStillOnTheEyeCannotCompleteTheHandover();
ANonZeroHandoverDelayHoldsTheHandoverOpen();
StopEndsTheRunFromWhereverItIs();
ANonZeroDecelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStopping();
ADriveTripStopsTheBeltAtOnceAndLatchesTheFault();
AFaultedConveyorCannotBeStarted();
ResetReleasesTheLatchAndMakesTheRunStartableAgain();
AStandingDriveFaultCannotBeAcknowledgedAway();
SpeedPercentageScalesTheCommandedVelocity();
MotorRunOnKeepsTheBeltTurningAfterTheDemandDrops();
ContainersPassedIsALifetimeTotal();
SensorSnapshotPublishesTheDetectionPoint();
TheInfeedInstanceRunsTheSharedMachineOnItsOwnRecipe();]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="ConveyorPowersUpStoppedWithNothingCounted" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000002}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A run nobody has started must be stopped, unfaulted and claiming no
// history. INIT being ordinal zero is what makes that true without an
// initialiser, so an instance that is never configured still powers up safe
// rather than in whichever state happens to be first in the enum.
METHOD PRIVATE ConveyorPowersUpStoppedWithNothingCounted
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ConveyorPowersUpStoppedWithNothingCounted');

conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.INIT,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'fresh conveyor state');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
            Message := 'fresh conveyor reported a turning belt');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
            Message := 'fresh conveyor reported a motor fault');

AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 0,
                  Actual := conveyor.ContainersPassed,
                  Message := 'fresh conveyor ContainersPassed');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 0.0,
                   Actual := conveyor.CommandedVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'fresh conveyor CommandedVelocity');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="StartRampsTheConveyorUpToWaitingForAContainer" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000003}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The drawn Start and "Drive at speed" arcs. STARTING is a state of its own
// rather than a jump straight to WAIT_CONTAINER, so a detection that arrives
// while the belt is still coming up to speed cannot be treated as a container
// that has been transported.
METHOD PRIVATE StartRampsTheConveyorUpToWaitingForAContainer
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('StartRampsTheConveyorUpToWaitingForAContainer');

conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe, Start := TRUE);
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STARTING,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'Start did not reach STARTING');

AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
           Message := 'the belt was not driven while ramping up');

conveyor();
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a zero AccelTime ramp did not complete');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ANonZeroAccelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStarting" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000004}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The far end of the AccelTime gate. The ramp is a DURATION, not a cycle
// count: no number of scans may complete it while the clock stands still, or
// a fast task would declare a heavy belt up to speed sooner than a slow one.
METHOD PRIVATE ANonZeroAccelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStarting
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ANonZeroAccelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStarting');

recipe.AccelTime := T#500ms;
conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe, Start := TRUE);

FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STARTING,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the ramp completed on scan count rather than on time');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="DetectionHoldsTheContainerUntilDownstreamIsReady" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000005}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The drawn Detection arc, and the not(downstream ready) self-loop after it.
// The belt is DROPPED here on purpose: a container held against a station
// that will not take it must stop rather than be pushed into it.
METHOD PRIVATE DetectionHoldsTheContainerUntilDownstreamIsReady
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('DetectionHoldsTheContainerUntilDownstreamIsReady');

DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

BlockTheEye(sensor := sensor);
conveyor();
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_DOWNSTREAM_READY,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a detected container did not reach WAIT_DOWNSTREAM_READY');

FOR i := 1 TO 5 DO
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_DOWNSTREAM_READY,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the container left without downstream ever going ready');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
            Message := 'the belt kept turning against a station that was not ready');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="DownstreamReadyReleasesTheContainerIntoTheHandover" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000006}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The drawn "downstream ready" arc. Entering PROCES_CONTAINER has to start
// the belt again in the same scan, or the container would sit still through a
// hand-over the next station believes is under way.
METHOD PRIVATE DownstreamReadyReleasesTheContainerIntoTheHandover
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('DownstreamReadyReleasesTheContainerIntoTheHandover');

DriveToHandover(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.PROCES_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a ready station did not release the container');

AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
           Message := 'the belt was not restarted for the hand-over');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AWithdrawnDownstreamPutsTheContainerBackOnHold" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000007}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The drawn not(downstream ready) arc as a retreat out of the hand-over.
// DownstreamReady is a level and the next station may drop it at any moment;
// a container that is still on the eye when that happens has not gone
// anywhere yet, so it goes back to being held rather than being pushed into a
// station that has stopped taking.
METHOD PRIVATE AWithdrawnDownstreamPutsTheContainerBackOnHold
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AWithdrawnDownstreamPutsTheContainerBackOnHold');

DriveToHandover(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

conveyor(DownstreamReady := FALSE);

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_DOWNSTREAM_READY,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a withdrawn station did not put the container back on hold');

AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 0,
                  Actual := conveyor.ContainersPassed,
                  Message := 'an abandoned hand-over counted a container');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AClearedEyeCompletesTheHandoverAndCountsTheContainer" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000008}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The drawn "Container received" and "Conveyor cleared" labels, which are one
// arc here: the next station has it AND this run is empty are the same
// observation from the two ends of the transfer, and the module only knows
// either of them through the eye going clear. It is also the only place a
// container is ever counted. Counting on the completed hand-over rather
// than on the detection is what makes ContainersPassed mean "handed to the
// next station" instead of "seen at some point".
METHOD PRIVATE AClearedEyeCompletesTheHandoverAndCountsTheContainer
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AClearedEyeCompletesTheHandoverAndCountsTheContainer');

DriveToHandover(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

ClearTheEye(sensor := sensor);
conveyor();

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a completed hand-over did not return to WAIT_CONTAINER');

AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 1,
                  Actual := conveyor.ContainersPassed,
                  Message := 'the handed-over container was not counted');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AContainerStillOnTheEyeCannotCompleteTheHandover" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000009}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The negation in the hand-over guard, pinned from the failing side. A
// hand-over that could complete with the container still breaking the eye
// would count containers that never left the run, and the count is what the
// unit above reports as throughput.
METHOD PRIVATE AContainerStillOnTheEyeCannotCompleteTheHandover
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AContainerStillOnTheEyeCannotCompleteTheHandover');

DriveToHandover(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

FOR i := 1 TO 5 DO
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.PROCES_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hand-over completed with the container still on the eye');

AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 0,
                  Actual := conveyor.ContainersPassed,
                  Message := 'a container still on the eye was counted');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ANonZeroHandoverDelayHoldsTheHandoverOpen" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000000a}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The far end of the drawn Delay gate. With the eye clear and the delay
// running, no number of scans may finish the hand-over while the clock stands
// still - otherwise the gap between two closely spaced containers would read
// as a completed hand-over on a fast enough task.
METHOD PRIVATE ANonZeroHandoverDelayHoldsTheHandoverOpen
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ANonZeroHandoverDelayHoldsTheHandoverOpen');

recipe.HandoverDelay := T#200ms;
DriveToHandover(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

ClearTheEye(sensor := sensor);
FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.PROCES_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hand-over delay expired on scan count rather than on time');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="StopEndsTheRunFromWhereverItIs" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000000b}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The drawn Stop arc, which leaves every state rather than one. It is decided
// above the CASE for that reason: a Stop that any single state could decline
// would not be a Stop, and the state holding a container mid-hand-over is
// exactly the one that would be tempted to decline it.
METHOD PRIVATE StopEndsTheRunFromWhereverItIs
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('StopEndsTheRunFromWhereverItIs');

DriveToHandover(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.PROCES_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'setup did not reach the hand-over');

conveyor(Start := FALSE, Stop := TRUE);
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STOPPING,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'Stop was declined mid-hand-over');

conveyor();
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.INIT,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a zero DecelTime ramp did not complete');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
            Message := 'the belt was still turning after the run had stopped');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ANonZeroDecelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStopping" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000000c}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The far end of the DecelTime gate, and the reason STOPPING is a state at
// all. A run that reached INIT before the belt had actually stopped could be
// restarted into a drive that was still coasting the other way.
METHOD PRIVATE ANonZeroDecelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStopping
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ANonZeroDecelTimeHoldsTheConveyorInStopping');

recipe.DecelTime := T#800ms;
DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

conveyor(Start := FALSE, Stop := TRUE);
FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STOPPING,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the stop ramp completed on scan count rather than on time');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ADriveTripStopsTheBeltAtOnceAndLatchesTheFault" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000000d}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A trip is not a hand-over. The belt has to drop in the same scan the fault
// is seen - the run-on that lets a released container coast clear must not
// double as a reason for a faulted belt to keep turning - and the fault has
// to outlive the drive-side condition that raised it, or a run would restart
// itself after a trip nobody ever saw.
METHOD PRIVATE ADriveTripStopsTheBeltAtOnceAndLatchesTheFault
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ADriveTripStopsTheBeltAtOnceAndLatchesTheFault');

recipe.MotorRunOn := T#500ms;
DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);
AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
           Message := 'setup did not get the belt turning');

axis(DriveFault := TRUE);
conveyor();

AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
           Message := 'a drive trip did not raise MotorFault');

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STOPPING,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a drive trip did not end the run');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
            Message := 'the run-on kept a faulted belt turning');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 0.0,
                   Actual := conveyor.CommandedVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'a faulted conveyor still commanded a speed');

axis(DriveFault := FALSE);
conveyor();
AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
           Message := 'the fault cleared itself when the drive condition went away');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AFaultedConveyorCannotBeStarted" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000000e}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The latch has to gate the Start arc as well as force the stop, or a run
// that had tripped and settled in INIT would take the next Start as if
// nothing had happened - which is the same restart-by-itself the latch exists
// to prevent, one state later.
METHOD PRIVATE AFaultedConveyorCannotBeStarted
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AFaultedConveyorCannotBeStarted');

axis(DriveFault := TRUE);
conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe);
axis(DriveFault := FALSE);

conveyor(Start := TRUE);
conveyor();

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.INIT,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a faulted conveyor accepted a Start');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
            Message := 'a faulted conveyor drove its belt');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ResetReleasesTheLatchAndMakesTheRunStartableAgain" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000000f}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The PackML Reset is the single point at which a tripped run becomes usable
// again, and it has to reach the drive as well as the latch: releasing the
// latch alone would leave the module willing to start against an axis still
// refusing to move.
METHOD PRIVATE ResetReleasesTheLatchAndMakesTheRunStartableAgain
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ResetReleasesTheLatchAndMakesTheRunStartableAgain');

recipe.SpeedPercentage := 100.0;
axis(DriveFault := TRUE);
conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe);
axis(DriveFault := FALSE);

conveyor(Reset := TRUE);
AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
            Message := 'Reset did not release the motor fault');

conveyor(Reset := FALSE, Start := TRUE);
conveyor();

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a reset conveyor did not start');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 1000.0,
                   Actual := axis.ActualVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the drive was never acknowledged, so it did not move');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AStandingDriveFaultCannotBeAcknowledgedAway" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000010}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The latch is reset-dominant, so a Reset held against a fault that is still
// standing does release it - for exactly as long as the Reset is held. The
// moment the operator lets go, the drive re-raises it and the latch takes it
// back. That is the drive's answer rather than the latch's, and it is what
// stops an acknowledgement from being mistaken for a repair.
METHOD PRIVATE AStandingDriveFaultCannotBeAcknowledgedAway
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AStandingDriveFaultCannotBeAcknowledgedAway');

axis(DriveFault := TRUE);
conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe);
AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
           Message := 'setup did not latch the fault');

conveyor(Reset := TRUE);
AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
            Message := 'the reset-dominant latch did not release while Reset was held');

axis(DriveFault := TRUE);
conveyor(Reset := FALSE);
AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorFault,
           Message := 'a standing drive fault did not come back after the acknowledgement');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="SpeedPercentageScalesTheCommandedVelocity" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000011}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The recipe carries a PERCENTAGE rather than drive units, so a run that is
// re-geared during commissioning keeps its recipe and only its rated velocity
// changes. The scaling therefore has to happen inside the module and reach
// the axis, not be pre-computed by whoever fills in the recipe.
METHOD PRIVATE SpeedPercentageScalesTheCommandedVelocity
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('SpeedPercentageScalesTheCommandedVelocity');

recipe.SpeedPercentage := 37.5;
conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe, Start := TRUE);

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 375.0,
                   Actual := conveyor.CommandedVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'CommandedVelocity did not scale the rated velocity');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 375.0,
                   Actual := axis.ActualVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the commanded velocity never reached the drive');

conveyor(Start := FALSE, Stop := TRUE);
AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 0.0,
                   Actual := axis.ActualVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the drive kept its demand after the run stopped');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="MotorRunOnKeepsTheBeltTurningAfterTheDemandDrops" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000012}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The engaged side of the run-on, which needs no clock: while the window is
// open the belt must stay driven however many scans pass. Without it a
// container released on the last scan of a hand-over would stop half on the
// transfer, which is the jam the run-on exists to prevent.
METHOD PRIVATE MotorRunOnKeepsTheBeltTurningAfterTheDemandDrops
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('MotorRunOnKeepsTheBeltTurningAfterTheDemandDrops');

recipe.SpeedPercentage := 80.0;
recipe.MotorRunOn := T#300ms;
DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

// Detection drops the demand: the container is held for the next station.
BlockTheEye(sensor := sensor);
conveyor();

FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.MotorRunning,
           Message := 'the run-on window closed on scan count rather than on time');

AssertEquals_LREAL(Expected := 800.0,
                   Actual := axis.ActualVelocity,
                   Delta := 0.001,
                   Message := 'the belt was still called running but no longer driven');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ContainersPassedIsALifetimeTotal" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000013}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// The count is the run's lifetime throughput, not a per-cycle flag: it
// survives every return to WAIT_CONTAINER, and clearing it is a supervisory
// action rather than something a state change may do quietly.
METHOD PRIVATE ContainersPassedIsALifetimeTotal
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('ContainersPassedIsALifetimeTotal');

DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

FOR i := 1 TO 3 DO
	BlockTheEye(sensor := sensor);
	conveyor(DownstreamReady := TRUE);
	conveyor();

	ClearTheEye(sensor := sensor);
	conveyor();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 3,
                  Actual := conveyor.ContainersPassed,
                  Message := 'three hand-overs did not add up to three containers');

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the run did not settle back on WAIT_CONTAINER');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="SensorSnapshotPublishesTheDetectionPoint" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000014}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Sensors is what an HMI or a trace line reads instead of reaching through
// the equipment module into a sensor block. Slot 1 has to agree with the
// injected sensor on the same scan, and the reserved slots have to stay at
// their defaults - a run that filled all five from its one point would report
// four containers that do not exist.
METHOD PRIVATE SensorSnapshotPublishesTheDetectionPoint
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('SensorSnapshotPublishesTheDetectionPoint');

sensor.Simulation := TRUE;
sensor.Inverted := TRUE;
sensor.DebounceTime := T#5ms;
sensor(HardwareInput := FALSE);

conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe);

AssertEquals_BOOL(Expected := sensor.Active,
                  Actual := conveyor.Sensors[1].Active,
                  Message := 'snapshot slot 1 Active');

AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.Sensors[1].Inverted,
           Message := 'snapshot slot 1 Inverted');

AssertTrue(Condition := conveyor.Sensors[1].Simulated,
           Message := 'snapshot slot 1 Simulated');

AssertEquals_TIME(Expected := T#5ms,
                  Actual := conveyor.Sensors[1].DebounceTime,
                  Message := 'snapshot slot 1 DebounceTime');

AssertFalse(Condition := conveyor.Sensors[2].Inverted,
            Message := 'a reserved slot was filled from the detection point');

AssertEquals_TIME(Expected := T#0ms,
                  Actual := conveyor.Sensors[5].DebounceTime,
                  Message := 'a reserved slot was filled from the detection point');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="AContainerLiftedOffTheEyeReleasesTheHold" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000019}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// A container held for a station that will not take it can also simply stop
// existing - an operator lifts it off while clearing a jam. The hold has to
// end when it does, or the run would wait forever for a hand-over of nothing
// and the next real container would be counted as this one.
METHOD PRIVATE AContainerLiftedOffTheEyeReleasesTheHold
VAR
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('AContainerLiftedOffTheEyeReleasesTheHold');

DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

BlockTheEye(sensor := sensor);
conveyor();
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_DOWNSTREAM_READY,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'setup did not put a container on hold');

ClearTheEye(sensor := sensor);
conveyor();

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.WAIT_CONTAINER,
                 Actual := conveyor.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the hold outlived the container that caused it');

AssertEquals_UINT(Expected := 0,
                  Actual := conveyor.ContainersPassed,
                  Message := 'a container that was never handed over was counted');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="TheInfeedInstanceRunsTheSharedMachineOnItsOwnRecipe" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-00000000001a}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// FB_Conveyor only earns its place if an instance of it is a whole equipment
// module, so this pins the one thing FB_InfeedConveyor is: the shared state
// machine wired to this run's own sensor, drive and tuning. Its AccelTime is
// what proves the recipe is the instance's rather than the block's - the run
// stays in STARTING here where a default-tuned conveyor would already be
// waiting for a container.
METHOD PRIVATE TheInfeedInstanceRunsTheSharedMachineOnItsOwnRecipe
VAR
	infeed : FB_InfeedConveyor;
	i : INT;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[TEST('TheInfeedInstanceRunsTheSharedMachineOnItsOwnRecipe');

infeed();
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.INIT,
                 Actual := infeed.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the infeed run did not power up stopped');

infeed(Start := TRUE);
AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STARTING,
                 Actual := infeed.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the infeed run did not accept a Start');

FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
	infeed();
END_FOR

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STARTING,
                 Actual := infeed.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'the infeed run ignored its own AccelTime');

AssertTrue(Condition := infeed.MotorRunning,
           Message := 'the infeed belt was not driven while coming up to speed');

infeed(BeltDriveFault := TRUE);
AssertTrue(Condition := infeed.MotorFault,
           Message := 'the infeed drive fault line never reached the state machine');

AssertEquals_INT(Expected := E_ConveyorState.STOPPING,
                 Actual := infeed.CurrentState,
                 Message := 'a fault on the infeed drive did not end the run');

TEST_FINISHED();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="DriveToWaitContainer" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000015}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Arrangement shared by the cases that start from a belt already running with
// nothing on it. Binds both dependencies and the recipe, so a caller sets any
// recipe field it cares about BEFORE calling this, and holds Start - the run
// is meant to stay up until the case takes it down.
//
// The detection point is put into simulation with no debounce: this suite is
// exercising the CONVEYOR, and a filter window on the sensor would put a
// second timer between the level a case sets and the arc it is asserting.
METHOD PRIVATE DriveToWaitContainer
VAR_IN_OUT
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[sensor.Simulation := TRUE;
sensor.DebounceTime := T#0ms;
sensor(HardwareInput := FALSE);

conveyor(caseDetectionSensor := sensor, conveyorAxis := axis, Control := recipe, Start := TRUE);
conveyor();]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="DriveToHandover" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000016}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Arrangement shared by the cases about the hand-over itself: a container is
// on the eye and the next station has said it will take it, so the run is in
// PROCES_CONTAINER with DownstreamReady still held.
METHOD PRIVATE DriveToHandover
VAR_IN_OUT
	conveyor : FB_Conveyor;
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
	axis : FB_AxisBase;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
	recipe : ST_ConveyorControl;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[DriveToWaitContainer(conveyor := conveyor, sensor := sensor, axis := axis, recipe := recipe);

BlockTheEye(sensor := sensor);
conveyor();
conveyor(DownstreamReady := TRUE);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="BlockTheEye" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000017}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Puts a container in front of the detection point. Only the SENSOR is
// cycled: whether the conveyor gets to see the new level on this scan or the
// next is the sort of thing a case is often asserting, so it stays the
// caller's decision.
METHOD PRIVATE BlockTheEye
VAR_IN_OUT
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[sensor.SimulatedInput := TRUE;
sensor(HardwareInput := FALSE);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ClearTheEye" Id="{5e4501d0-0026-4d19-9a41-000000000018}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE ClearTheEye
VAR_IN_OUT
	sensor : FB_DigitalInput;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[sensor.SimulatedInput := FALSE;
sensor(HardwareInput := FALSE);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
